+## Art and palettes
+
+`graphics/glide/paraglider.png` is the indexed 64x256 build sheet: four 64x64
+poses, south/north/west/east. Individual pose PNGs are editing exports. The
+fixed runtime palette is `paraglider.gbapal`, with a matching `.pal` source.
+`item.png` is the 24x24 Bag icon.
+
+Foreground runtime assets live in `graphics/weather/kyoto_clouds/`. The
+`editing/` directory contains the large, medium and small PNGs and the complete
+indexed 64x704 cell sheet. Repack an edited cell sheet with Python/Pillow:
 
 ```sh
 python3 tools/rebuild_kyoto_clouds.py graphics/weather/kyoto_clouds/editing/cloud_cells.png graphics/weather/kyoto_clouds
 ```
 
-Keep index 0 transparent and silhouette shade slots 4..12 unchanged. The
-background atlas/maps are the existing prepacked runtime assets; the foreground
-repacker does not regenerate them.
-
-The optional lower surface renderer is configured in
-`include/kyoto_cloud_config.h`. Its default map predicate is Littleroot (group
-0, map 9); adjust it to the maps where you place the supplied solid-blue marker
-tile/palette. Only a nonzero tile filled with palette index 1, using the exact
-marker palette, is replaced. Other terrain sharing the palette is preserved.
-Normal metatiles can use the marker on BG2. Triple metatiles can use it on BG3,
-retaining their BG2 and BG1 artwork above the lower clouds.
-
-The lower layer reserves physical BG palette 13 and character-block-2 tiles
-0..255 on enabled maps. Kyoto/Opal map banks 0..12 are preserved. Native BG3
-artwork is copied into a 31-tile cache; complex views that exceed this cache
-fall back to their native static surface. Keep other tile animations and UI
-graphics out of the reserved range. UI windows which require that range need
-an explicit compatible allocation or the lower-layer fallback.
