-## Integration notes
-
-The source was ported from the 7 October Glide + Clouds package. Item data now
-uses expansion's `ItemInfo` and icon fields. Collision hooks preserve the
-fork's enum types and run before its stairs logic. Cloud preparation follows
-the Opal palette transaction; pending streamed tile graphics are consulted
-before they reach VRAM. Lower clouds are uploaded after native VBlank/DMA
-work, so a map transfer cannot overwrite the cloud output in the same frame.
-
-The foreground uses eleven 64x64 OBJ cells (704 OBJ tiles). The Paraglider uses
-one additional 64x64 OBJ allocation (64 tiles) and one palette tagged `0x11FE`.
-Keep that tag unique. Allocation failures must preserve native actors and
-collision. The cloud workspace uses approximately 49 KB of heap and is freed
-before full-screen menus allocate their work buffers. Custom menus need the
-same early cleanup entry point if they allocate before changing callback2.
-
-The lower mask raster runs as ARM code in IWRAM. Cached source-map indices let
-sub-pixel atlas phases update without reclassifying native tiles. A linker
-assertion reserves stack headroom: do not move more rendering code to IWRAM
-without retesting Bag, since menu routines also need that space.
-
-The ARM silhouette kernel runs from an 832-byte scratch buffer. Linker bounds
-checks guard its size. Animation masks use the sprite upload queued for the
-current OAM frame, preventing the old one-frame silhouette mismatch.
-
